IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pip-nouns`

-- PART 5 -- RATE OF PERSONAL INDEPENDENCE PAYMENT: regulation 24.
--
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. The prescribed weekly rates are figures in pounds; they are copied from the
-- text and each is a named rule with its source line. The rate of a component that a person is entitled to is
-- found elsewhere (regs 12 and 13, and for older claimants regs 26 and 26A); this module says how much a week
-- each rate is.

§ `Regulation 24: the prescribed weekly rates`

-- reg 24(1): the prescribed weekly rates of the daily living component for the purposes of section 78(3) of the Act
-- are (a) the standard rate, 76.70 pounds; and (b) the enhanced rate, 114.60 pounds.
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 s 78(3)
-- src:353 | (1) The prescribed weekly rates of the daily living component for the purposes of section 78(3) of the Act are—
-- src:354 | (a) the standard rate, £76.70; and
-- src:355 | (b) the enhanced rate, £114.60.
@ref reg 24(1)(a) (src:354)
`reg 24(1)(a): the weekly standard rate of the daily living component, in pounds` MEANS 76.70

@ref reg 24(1)(b) (src:355)
`reg 24(1)(b): the weekly enhanced rate of the daily living component, in pounds` MEANS 114.60

-- reg 24(2): the prescribed weekly rates of the mobility component for the purposes of section 79(3) of the Act are (a)
-- the standard rate, 30.30 pounds; and (b) the enhanced rate, 80.00 pounds.
-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 s 79(3)
-- src:356 | (2) The prescribed weekly rates of the mobility component for the purposes of section 79(3) of the Act are—
-- src:357 | (a) the standard rate, £30.30; and
-- src:358 | (b) the enhanced rate, £80.00.
@ref reg 24(2)(a) (src:357)
`reg 24(2)(a): the weekly standard rate of the mobility component, in pounds` MEANS 30.30

@ref reg 24(2)(b) (src:358)
`reg 24(2)(b): the weekly enhanced rate of the mobility component, in pounds` MEANS 80.00

-- The weekly amount of a rate of a component. A person with no rate of a component is entitled to no amount, and the
-- text prescribes none, so that case is not covered (NOTHING).
@ref reg 24(1), reg 24(2) (src:353, src:356)
GIVEN comp IS A `a component of personal independence payment`
      rate IS A `a rate of a component`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 24: the weekly rate, in pounds, of this component at this rate` comp `at` rate MEANS
    CONSIDER comp
    WHEN `the daily living component` THEN
        CONSIDER rate
        WHEN `the standard rate of the component` THEN JUST `reg 24(1)(a): the weekly standard rate of the daily living component, in pounds`
        WHEN `the enhanced rate of the component` THEN JUST `reg 24(1)(b): the weekly enhanced rate of the daily living component, in pounds`
        WHEN `no rate of the component` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `the mobility component` THEN
        CONSIDER rate
        WHEN `the standard rate of the component` THEN JUST `reg 24(2)(a): the weekly standard rate of the mobility component, in pounds`
        WHEN `the enhanced rate of the component` THEN JUST `reg 24(2)(b): the weekly enhanced rate of the mobility component, in pounds`
        WHEN `no rate of the component` THEN NOTHING
